.TH CONDUCTOR-SYNC 8 "2026-10-03" "Samba Conductor" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
conductor-sync \- provisioning from Samba AD to Google Workspace
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B conductor-sync
.I command
.RI [ flags ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B conductor-sync
reads users and groups from Samba Active Directory with a read-only account
and provisions them to Google Workspace. Every run computes a plan;
scheduled runs apply only plans inside the configured safety limits;
nothing is deleted automatically. Manual commands run as the
.B conductor-sync
user, for example
.BR "sudo \-u conductor-sync conductor-sync plan" .
Each command accepts
.BR \-h .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B plan
Compute and record a plan (read-only on both sides).
.TP
.B apply
Compute a fresh plan and apply it (confirmation, safety limits).
.TP
.B status
Mode, last runs, links, unfinished operations, audit chain.
.TP
.B history
Recent runs, or one run's plan and journal.
.TP
.B map
The AD object to target object links.
.TP
.B delete-user
Permanently delete one suspended, sync-owned account.
.TP
.B audit verify | audit export
Check or export the hash-chained audit log.
.TP
.B check-config
Validate the configuration and the credentials.
.TP
.B serve
Run the local management API used by conductor's web interface (started by
.BR conductor-sync-api.socket ).
.TP
.B config export | import | history
The sync and connection settings (versions; export never includes a secret).
.TP
.B key set | key show
The Google service account key (stored encrypted).
.TP
.B secret status | set NAME | remove NAME
The AD bind password (\fBad-bind-password\fR) and the alert webhook secret
(\fBalert-webhook-secret\fR), stored encrypted; the value is read from
standard input, never from the command line. \fBremove google-key\fR removes
the stored service account key.
.TP
.B version
Print the version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 done, 1 error, 2 usage, 3 blocked (safety limits, or before the first
manual apply), 4 partial, 5 not applied (declined, plan changed, delete
refused), 6 manual apply in dry-run mode.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/conductor-sync/conductor-sync.toml
Configuration.
.TP
.I /etc/conductor-sync/credentials/
.B state-key
(and, unless stored encrypted in the state database,
.BR ad-bind ),
loaded by systemd.
.TP
.I /var/lib/conductor-sync/
State database.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR conductor (8)
